    "description": "This episode of The Podcast Lane 10 in 10 series goes deeper than business. Host Pete the Peptide Guy sits down with returning guest Nic Magallanes for a raw unfiltered conversation about life adversity identity and what it truly means to build a legacy.\n\nNic steps away from the professional spotlight as a senior loan officer to share the real story behind the man. From a painful and misunderstood moment in high school that led to bullying and isolation to growing up in a broken home filled with chaos Nic opens up about the defining experiences that shaped his mindset and resilience.\n\nThis episode explores what hitting rock bottom really looks like and why it can become the foundation for personal growth. Nic shares how navigating trauma family struggles and a lack of support forced him to develop perseverance at a young age and how those lessons now fuel the way he shows up as a father husband and man.\n\nAt the core of this conversation is legacy. After losing his father and not having a close relationship growing up Nic made a conscious decision to break generational patterns and create something meaningful for his own son. This episode is a message to the next generation about perspective work ethic and understanding that adversity does not define your future.\n\nIf you have ever faced challenges questioned your path or needed a reminder of your strength this episode will resonate deeply.\n\nConnect and Learn More\nNic Magallanes, born in Lubbock, Texas, is a highly accomplished Marine Corps veteran, leader, and residential loan officer whose journey is defined by resilience, discipline, and service. After earning his Associate of Applied Science in Law Enforcement from South Plains College, Nic enlisted in the United States Marine Corps, ultimately serving 17 years and 9 months with deployments in support of Operation Iraqi Freedom and Operation National Resolution. Throughout his military career, he earned numerous commendations, including a Navy and Marine Corps Commendation Medal, multiple Achievement Medals, and recognition for exemplary conduct and marksmanship. Committed to personal growth, Nic went on to earn multiple advanced degrees, including master’s degrees in Administration of Justice & Security and General Psychology, while being inducted into prestigious honor societies. After retiring from the military, he transitioned into the mortgage industry in 2019, where he has successfully funded over 350 transactions and received multiple awards for top performance. Now based in Arizona, Nic continues to lead with purpose, driven by his commitment to family, legacy, and making a lasting impact.\n\nNicolas Magallanes Senior Loan Officer NMLS ID #1853487 Green Home Loans NMLS ID #2464753 Equal Housing Lender\n\nTake notes, get inspired, and think bigger.\n\nFollow The Podcast Lane for more real conversations with experts leaders and individuals who are making an impact in their field. Share this episode with someone who needs to hear it and help us continue to grow this powerful community. Your next level might just start here.\n\nBrought to you by The Podcast Lane",
