    "description": "Jen Shirkani brings powerful insight into the role emotional intelligence plays in effective leadership and long-term success.\n\nAs a nationally recognized expert on emotional intelligence, author of Ego vs. EQ and Choose Resilience, and host of the Ego vs. EQ podcast, Jen shares lessons drawn from more than 25 years of leadership development experience. Her work spans Fortune 50 companies, government agencies, universities, and organizations seeking to elevate performance through self-awareness and human-centered leadership.\n\nThe conversation explores how unchecked ego can limit growth, create blind spots, and impact culture—while emotional intelligence helps leaders build trust, resilience, and meaningful influence. Known for her relatable style, humor, and practical strategies, Jen offers actionable insights leaders can apply immediately.\n\nThis episode is a must-listen for executives, managers, and professionals who want to lead with clarity, connection, and greater impact in today’s evolving workplace.\n\n\n\nJoin the conversation in the comments and share this episode with someone ready to rethink marketing, life, business, community or what’s making a difference for others.\n\nThe Podcast Lane ~ Connecting People One Podcast at a Time",
