    "description": "Known as NANCYAF, Nancy A. Shenker knows a lot of things because she’s experienced a lot of things—across nearly 70 trips around the sun. A brand marketing powerhouse, digital marketing and AI pioneer, Nancy is the founder of theONswitch.com and the voice behind the podcast AgeBlind, where she challenges outdated narratives about age, relevance, and reinvention.\n\nIn this episode of The 10 in 10 with Nancy A. Shenker, Nancy breaks down what branding really is, why it matters more than ever in today’s AI-driven, attention-fragmented world, and how personal branding isn’t about age—it’s about clarity, courage, and consistency.\n\nNancy’s career spans C-suite leadership at Citibank, Mastercard, and Reed Exhibitions (producers of ComicCon), along with life as a founder, award-winning writer, innovator, rule-breaker, mentor, mom, nana, volunteer, and board member. On her 69th birthday, Nancy launched her personal brand—proving that relevance has no expiration date. Nancy brings wit, wisdom, and bold insight into what it means to build a brand—and a life—that stays switched on.\n\nThe 10 in 10 podcast, Nancy A. Shenker, NANCYAF, branding expert podcast, personal branding strategy, AI in marketing, digital marketing pioneer, AgeBlind podcast, women in branding, reinvention at any age",
